{"actor_ref":"claude","class":"draft_history","document_uuid":"01a1a54a-31af-755d-a6d8-6de3d396037c","id":"01a1a630-937e-7240-bb6f-ecd1547af910","idempotency_key":"2ac83caeac637d1e06eb6ce910c3282bcc49c42b707265aaba6a929d2c9a8240","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T10:52:43Z","payload":{"note":"Tournament persistence. Schema v8 adds 'tournaments' (id, name, format, status, state_json, pgn, created, updated) and 'tournament_standings' (a projection keyed by tournament and competitor), with the storage API in crates/rbc-db/src/tournament.rs and save/load/all/standings in crates/ai/src/tournament_store.rs. The state is one JSON blob because a tournament is a domain object and the database's job is to keep it whole; the standings are projected on every save so a leaderboard reads rows instead of replaying a bracket. Resume after restart is tested by round-tripping a cup mid-round and continuing to schedule from the loaded copy; a pause is stored as a decision, not a cache, so a paused cup comes back paused. Combined PGN carries Event/Round/Board/White/Black/Result per game plus the movetext and result on the game line. 26 tests in the tournament suite. Not built as a route or UI: t-a994 is the tournament UI ticket.","target":"t-3a41"},"type":"work.note_added","v":2}
